# {{NAME}}

Local Stagepass project for Webflow.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
npm run build
stagepass link {{NAME}}
```

`stagepass link` without `--origin` uses the hosts from `stagepass.json` (`origin` / optional `production`). Activate on your staging site: `https://{{STAGING_HOST}}/?stagepass={{NAME}}.sp`

## Scripts

| Script | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `npm run build` | Bundle JS/CSS into `dist/` with content hashes, SRI, and `manifest.json` |
| `npm run watch` | Rebuild on change |
| `npm run dev` | Alias of `watch` (until a real HMR server ships) |

## Webflow Custom Code

Prefer the major CDN pin `@2`. An exact pin is optional (see `data-stagepass-version`).

### Head

```html
{{HEAD_SNIPPET}}
```

Optional exact pin (replace `@2` in the URL if you need a locked version): `@{{LOADER_VERSION}}`.

### Footer

```html
{{FOOTER_SNIPPET}}
```

After each production upload, set `data-src` / `data-href` to your hosted URLs. For content-hashed uploads, read `file` from `dist/manifest.json`. Local Stagepass swapping can keep using the stable `dist/main.js` and `dist/styles.css` copies.

### Subresource Integrity (SRI)

`npm run build` writes a sha384 `integrity` per output in `dist/manifest.json`:

```json
{
  "main.js": {
    "file": "main.a1b2c3d4.js",
    "integrity": "sha384-..."
  },
  "styles.css": {
    "file": "styles.e5f6a7b8.css",
    "integrity": "sha384-..."
  }
}
```

Use those values on production tags (and keep `crossorigin="anonymous"` when the asset host sends CORS headers):

```html
<script
  src="https://cdn.example.com/{{NAME}}/main.a1b2c3d4.js"
  integrity="sha384-..."
  crossorigin="anonymous"
  data-stagepass
  data-src="https://cdn.example.com/{{NAME}}/main.a1b2c3d4.js"
  data-stagepass-path="/dist/main.js"
></script>
```

